  "transcript": "Provider: Hello.\nPatient: Nice shirt.\nProvider: Yeah, sure.\nPatient: Like, what the hell is he looking at?\nProvider: All right. So, uh, what hurts the most?\nPatient: My throat.\nProvider: Okay.\nPatient: And my ears. I was here like two or three weeks ago.\nProvider: Mhm.\nPatient: And the other doctor said I had pneumonia.\nProvider: Mhm.\nPatient: She treated me for that. I really never got really 100% better.\nProvider: Mhm.\nPatient: And then this came on like three days ago and it's not getting better, so.\nProvider: Okay. Well, let's get you checked out.\nProvider: Deep breath in and out.\nProvider: Good.\nProvider: All right, just breathe normal.\nProvider: So when you say your pneumonia didn't really completely resolve, what do you mean by that?\nPatient: I don't know. It never got really better. Like, I still had a cough and I still have a cough now.\nProvider: Mhm.\nPatient: It's like I never coughed anything up. I don't know why, but.\nProvider: Okay.\nProvider: And I had a ear infection last time I was here.\nProvider: And today, do both your ears hurt or just one?\nPatient: They both hurt. That one hurts more than this one.\nProvider: Okay.\nProvider: Open up.\nProvider: Any pain in this area?\nPatient: A little tender.\nProvider: On both sides?\nPatient: On the right, on my right side.\nProvider: Over here?\nPatient: Yeah.\nProvider: Okay.\nProvider: And no tenderness back here?\nPatient: No.\nProvider: Good.\nProvider: Any sinus tenderness?\nPatient: No.\nProvider: Good. How about up here?\nPatient: No.\nProvider: Good.\nPatient: Actually, it feels good.\nProvider: All right. And she took x-rays last time?\nPatient: Yes.\nProvider: Okay.\nProvider: Well, did she say your lungs sounded bad?\nPatient: Yeah, she said there was a crackling.\nProvider: Okay. Well, your lungs sound good today.\nPatient: Well, good. I'm breathing better.\nProvider: Mhm.\nPatient: Like when I came here two weeks ago, I could I could barely breathe.\nProvider: Yeah.\nProvider: Um, so sometimes it can take a little while to get over, um, pneumonia, so you can have residual, um, shortness of breath, things like that. Um, your lungs sound nice and clear, though.\nPatient: Oh, good.\nProvider: Um, but yeah, you definitely have some stuff going on in the ears. Um, and we'll take care of that, so.\nPatient: Okay.\nProvider: Um, throat doesn't look bad. So, but, um, what we're going to do is we're going to give you a test. Um, did she test you last time you were here?\nPatient: No.\nProvider: Okay. So,\nPatient: I don't think she tested me for anything, but.\nProvider: Well, just let you know, COVID's on the rise, uh, unfortunately, so we're going to test you for that real quick. Um, and flu, um, and, uh, so, and we'll go from there. All right?\nPatient: Okay.\nProvider: Thanks, that's that.\nPatient: Oh, thank you.",
